      <meta name="description" its:translate="yes">Learn the systematic methodology to identify bottlenecks and optimize SUSE Linux Enterprise Server performance using data-driven tuning adjustments</meta>

      <abstract>
        <para>System tuning on &productname; is the systematic process of monitoring, analyzing, and adjusting operating system parameters and hardware configurations to optimize performance for specific application workloads. By leveraging tools like tuned and cpupower, administrators can eliminate system bottlenecks, improve resource allocation, and achieve optimal throughput and latency without compromising stability.</para>
<para><emphasis>Prerequisites</emphasis></para>
<itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para>Basic understanding of Linux commands, processes, daemons, and control groups</para>
</listitem>
<listitem>
<para>At least 24 hours of baseline performance data collected during normal operations</para>
</listitem>
<listitem>
<para>A verified system backup or snapshot</para>
</listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Functional diagnostic packages including sysstat, procps, and util-linux]</para>
</listitem>
</itemizedlist>
      </abstract>
